  (text "FINDER PUCK\nESP32-S3 swaps GPS positions with its partner over LoRa (RFM95W, 915 MHz), reads heading\nfrom LIS2MDL + LIS3DH, and draws a radar arrow and distance on a 1.28in round GC9A01 LCD (J3).\nLCD: own SPI host, SCK IO40, MOSI IO41, CS IO42, D/C IO21, RST IO47, backlight PWM IO48 -> Q2.\nLED1-LED4 strobe as a beacon; the motor pulses faster as the partner gets closer.\nPower: 1S LiPo on J2, charged from USB-C by U6 (state on IO6, USB on IO15); SW2 turns on Q3, which feeds VSYS; U7 makes 3.3 V.\nFlash over USB-C (native USB). Hold SW1 (IO0) while plugging in to force download mode.\nJ3 pin 1 is on the 3 o'clock side after the FPC folds under the glass: CONFIRM on a sample panel." (at 22.86 256.54 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 248156d0-04fb-50bd-beb9-1696361febb4)
  )
